{"kind":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The suffix automaton of a text: the smallest deterministic automaton that accepts every suffix"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"of it, whose paths from the start state spell exactly the text’s substrings (Blumer et al.,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“The Smallest Automaton Recognizing the Subwords of a Text”, 1985)."}],"topicSections":[{"generated":true,"title":"Structures","anchor":"Structures","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/CommonSubstring","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/TransitionsView-swift.struct"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/init(_:)"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Properties","anchor":"Instance-Properties","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/count","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/distinctSubstringCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/stateCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionCount","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionsView-swift.property"]},{"generated":true,"title":"Instance Methods","anchor":"Instance-Methods","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/contains(_:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/firstOccurrence(of:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/hasSuffix(_:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/longestCommonSubstring(with:)","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/occurrenceCount(of:)"]}],"primaryContentSections":[{"declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"tokens":[{"kind":"attribute","text":"@frozen"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"struct"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"identifier","text":"SuffixAutomaton"},{"kind":"text","text":"<"},{"kind":"genericParameter","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":"> "},{"kind":"keyword","text":"where"},{"kind":"text","text":" "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Symbol"},{"kind":"text","text":" : "},{"kind":"typeIdentifier","text":"Hashable","preciseIdentifier":"s:SH"}],"platforms":["Linux"]}],"kind":"declarations"},{"content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"overview","text":"Overview","level":2},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"It is built one symbol at a time in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":") expected steps, with at most 2"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" − 1 states and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"3"},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":" − 4 transitions. Each state stands for the substrings that end at the same set of places"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"in the text; its suffix link leads to the state of the longest of their suffixes that ends at"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"more places. A pattern is checked in O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"m"}]},{"type":"text","text":") transitions."}]},{"type":"codeListing","syntax":"swift","code":["let automaton = SuffixAutomaton(\"abcbc\")","automaton.contains(\"cbc\")              \/\/ true","automaton.occurrenceCount(of: \"bc\")    \/\/ 2","automaton.firstOccurrence(of: \"cb\")    \/\/ 2 ..< 4","automaton.distinctSubstringCount       \/\/ 12","automaton.longestCommonSubstring(with: \"xbcbz\")?.textRange  \/\/ 1 ..< 4, \"bcb\""]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Transitions from a state come in the order of their symbols: sorted when "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Symbol"},{"type":"text","text":" is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Comparable"},{"type":"text","text":", otherwise in the order the symbols first occur in the text. The automaton is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"directed graph, "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton\/transitionsView-swift.property","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":", and its suffix links are a tree that converts to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Grafluent’s "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":" with "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence(_:)"},{"type":"text","text":"."}]}],"kind":"content"}],"relationshipsSections":[{"title":"Conforms To","kind":"relationships","type":"conformsTo","identifiers":["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/s16SendableMetatypeP"]}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentation\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/suffixstructures\/suffixautomaton"]}],"metadata":{"fragments":[{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"SuffixAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"remoteSource":{"fileName":"SuffixAutomaton.swift","url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/GrafluentCollections\/blob\/main\/Sources\/SuffixStructures\/SuffixAutomaton.swift#L24"},"title":"SuffixAutomaton","navigatorTitle":[{"text":"SuffixAutomaton","kind":"identifier"}],"roleHeading":"Structure","externalID":"s:16SuffixStructures0A9AutomatonV","modules":[{"name":"SuffixStructures"}],"symbolKind":"struct","role":"symbol"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[["doc:\/\/SuffixStructures\/documentati